 "result": "maze.py is a level-synchronous BFS over a padded bytearray grid. Walls are pre-marked by translating '#' to visited, and the search stops as soon as E is reached. It reads stdin, prints the shortest 4-neighbour path length or -1, and handles missing S/E. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78), and assay accepted it as the baseline (2.737, noise 2.4%). Its earlier variant won +31% over the original list-based BFS. I'm resting here rather than spending more energy on further micro-optimisation.",
